50,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,Candidate A seems safe. Local items mean less shipping and likely less weight than stone.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"A and C both offer the ""human presence"" visitors love. A has demonstrations; C has a working bench.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Rin,,C is out! The conservation lab is already drowning; we can't put a working bench in the gallery.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Kenji,,B has too many loans from partner collections. That's a paperwork and transport nightmare.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,D is a financial and maintenance trap. Powered works and overhead rigging sound expensive and fragile.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Rin, you're right about C. A is much better for the staff and the space.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"If C is out, A is the strongest for attendance. Local craftspeople provide that live element.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Rin,,I love A! The town history volunteers would be perfect for helping with local weaving and dyeing.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Kenji,,A avoids the shipping cut-off issues of B and the mechanical failures of D.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,A is the most fiscally responsible choice. Local sourcing minimizes transport and mount costs.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I feel comfortable voting for A. It fits the room and the schedule.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Toshio,,I agree. It satisfies the visitor data without risking the infrastructure.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Rin,,It's the only one that doesn't make me worry about the staff!,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I'm in. A is the safest and most reliable bet.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"It appears we have reached a rare, unanimous consensus.","{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
